ers not much in the same way that  cyborg can control the stock market with  a wave of his hand flash could also  control time in the same manner and it  very much brought two of the most  underrated characters together and  showed just how powerful that they were  cyborg would of course go on to defeat  the forces of darkseid and after seeing  the league united in front of him he  decides to halt the invasion of earth  which of course wouldn't be possible  without the flash now because of this  moment we know that barry is one of the  most important characters in the dc  universe and realistically he's the only  person that can stop the nightmare  scenario that we see play out at the end  of the movie a version of barry of  course visited bruce in the cave during  the events of batman v superman and him  carrying out this action in the finale  let us know why it's so important that  he's there in the epilogue now this of  course has massive repercussions for the  future of the dc eu and we now know that  this immense power makes barry wonder  what else he can change in the  flashpoint comic book barry traveled  back in time to save his mother from  being murdered but this broke the  timeline and he ended up in an alternate  universe with a different version of  batman judging from what we know of the  upcoming flash movie both michael keaton  and ben affleck will be playing the dark  knight and this is likely because barry  was tempted by this power to go and  change more than just the events of the  steppenwolf fight his father was of  course in jail and the words he told him  rattled through his head as he ran so it  just makes so much sense that he would  go back and try and change things to  benefit his old dad now this is why the  scene is perfect to me not only is it a  beautiful piece of cinema that has  amazing music cgi and also  cinematography but it also propels a  person who was cast to the side in the  theatrical cut to the level of being a  god barry 